[
  {
    "id": "b2c0de0000000001", "type": "comment", "name": "NDI live preview on a web page: read me",
    "info": "Shows a live, silent preview of an NDI source on a small web page at\n`<httpNodeRoot>/ndi-example/live` (with default settings: http://<node-red>:1880/ndi-example/live).\n\n1. Open the **ndi live** node, press **Find sources** and pick your source (the example name is made up).\n2. Deploy, then open the page. The node connects to the source only while someone is watching.\n3. **stop** ends every viewer and refuses new ones; **start** allows them again.\n\nThe node sends the path of its stream when the flow starts; the page uses that path in an `<img>` tag.\nThe same `<img>` works in any dashboard template.\nAnyone who can reach Node-RED's HTTP endpoints can watch, unless your settings set `httpNodeAuth`.\n\nNeeds the NDI Runtime on the Node-RED computer (https://ndi.video/tools/).",
    "x": 220, "y": 60, "wires": []
  },
  {
